# Project Rules

This project keeps its rules in `.ai/rules/` so every AI agent reads the same
source. Nothing is duplicated here.

Before planning or editing any file, you MUST:

1. Open `.ai/rules/index.md` — it maps file globs to rule files.
2. Read every rule file whose globs cover the path(s) you are about to touch.
3. Run `grep -rin '<keyword>' .ai/rules` to catch rules a path match alone misses.

Do not write code until you are following every matching rule.

Wider project context lives alongside it:

- `.ai/context/` — what Ciian is and the build roadmap.
- `.ai/shapes/` — the JSON contracts for table and component shapes.
- `.ai/chores/` — step-by-step feature recipes.

See `.ai/README.md` for the full map.
